Carafe: the runtime log and the per-game mirror keep a finite byte budget, 512 MiB in all by
default, so a verbose run cannot fill the card. Every byte written to either sink is counted,
the start-up copy included, and each sink gets half; urgent lines and final records have reserves.
Nothing seeks, stats or flushes per line, and no live stream is truncated.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

